# Angular components

This app uses Angular 22 standalone components. Do not add NgModules or `standalone: true` (it is the default).

## Components

- Feature pages: class name `XPage`, files `x.ts` / `x.html` / `x.scss`, no selector (routed).
- Shared UI: selector `ui-*` (`UiPanel`, `UiIcon`, …), `input()` signals, BEM class names.
- Template control flow: `@if`, `@for` (with `track`), `@switch` — not `*ngIf` / `*ngFor`.
- DI: `inject()` in the field or constructor. Expose template data as `protected readonly`.
- Prefer `signal()` for UI state (`sidebarOpen`). Keep page data as imported constants unless it changes.

```typescript
@Component({
  imports: [RouterLink, UiPanel],
  styleUrl: './contact.scss',
  templateUrl: './contact.html',
})
export class ContactPage {
  protected readonly profile = PROFILE;
}
```

## Routing

- Register pages with `loadComponent: () => import('…').then((m) => m.XPage)`.
- Set `data: { title: '…' }` for the shell title.
- Bind public URLs with `routerLink`, not `href`, for in-app navigation.

## Tests

- Vitest + `TestBed`. Provide `SITE_CONFIG` and `provideRouter` when the shell or pages need them.
